Z||000016||ChopTop||11-14-2001||08:30 AM||||Check this thread for pics of my car: <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000002/HTML/20010924-1-006355.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000002/HTML/20010924-1-006355.html</A> <P>I'm switching over to the smooth moulding, the red bumper is from a 88GT.  Also when Archie did the chop I had him install a factory sunroof.  I'm going to (finally) try and get the car painted by next summer.  It has Suspension Techniques springs and Berreta wheels, I'm hoping to pick up new wheels too.||||reg||1
Z||000017||sqoach||11-14-2001||11:02 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by jch82:<BR><B>Here's a pic of choptop's fiero at the Lansing get together we had a while back!<P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/choptop_driverside(forum).jpg">   <P>Josh    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey ChopTop, what happened to your chin spoiler? Did you sell it? Did you hit a curb? Is this picture before you put it on? Where did you get it, anyway?<P>Sorry for all the questions. I just want one!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Oh yeah, how much did the ST's drop the car front and rear?<p>[This message has been edited by sqoach (edited 11-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000018||ChopTop||11-14-2001||11:34 AM||||Sqoach: I bought that spoiler around 1991-2.  It actually was part of a Fiero body kit, the spoiler was the only thing I liked.  FOCOA now sells the design as the Kid Danger.  It's normally on my 85GT that I converted to a fastback, held on with....velcro.  Considering I've ripped it off several times mainly by entering and exiting driveways, I'm glad I used that method.  <BR>ST lowering springs dropped the front of my car approximately 1 1/2 in the front and 2 inches in the rear.||||reg||1
